# 🧹 DATA CLEANING

## 🔢 Numerical Missing Values

Numerical missing values were handled using **Mean Imputation**.

| 🔧 Method | 🎯 Purpose |
|---|---|
| Mean Imputation | Fill missing numerical values |

---

## 🏷️ Categorical Missing Values

Categorical missing values were handled using the **Most Frequent** strategy.

| 🔧 Method | 🎯 Purpose |
|---|---|
| Most Frequent | Fill missing categorical values |

---

## 🤝 KNN Imputation

KNN Imputation was applied to selected numerical trip features.

| 📊 Feature |
|---|
| ⏱️ Duration |
| 📏 Distance |
| 💰 Fare |

---

## 📅 Date Standardization

The ride date was converted into a consistent **datetime format**.

This allowed useful time-based features such as hour, day and month to be extracted.

---

## 🚫 Unrealistic Records

Unrealistic records were removed from the dataset.

| ❌ Data Issue | 🧹 Action |
|---|---|
| Negative Fare | Removed |
| Zero Distance + Positive Fare | Removed |

---

# 🚨 OUTLIER HANDLING

Multiple methods were used to identify and reduce the effect of unusual values.

<table>

<tr>
<th>🔍 Method</th>
<th>📊 Feature</th>
<th>🎯 Purpose</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>📍 Z-Score</td>
<td>Fare & Distance</td>
<td>Detect unusual values</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>📦 IQR</td>
<td>Duration</td>
<td>Identify outliers</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>✂️ Winsorization</td>
<td>Fare</td>
<td>Reduce effect of extreme values</td>
</tr>

</table>

---

## 📊 Before vs After Winsorization

Fare values were compared before and after Winsorization.

| 📌 Stage | 💰 Fare Values |
|---|---|
| 🔵 Before | Original fare distribution |
| 🟢 After | Extreme values limited |

This helped reduce the influence of extreme fare values.

